; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Cantor Set
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     recursion, fractal, lines, levels
; SUMMARY:  Draws the Cantor set by removing the middle third of each line again and again.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Starts with one long bar. Underneath it, the middle third is
;   taken away, leaving two bars. Under each of those the middle
;   third goes again, and so on. Seven rows show the set taking shape.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the last line to draw more or fewer rows.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * recursion with two calls
;   * passing a level number down and counting it toward zero
;   * using SETXY to place each piece exactly
;   * painting rectangles with FILLED
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Draw 9 rows. Why do the bars almost vanish?
;   * Keep the outer quarters instead of the outer thirds.
;   * Give every row its own color using the level number.
; ============================================================

; CANTOR draws a bar from x to x + len at height y, then the two
; outer thirds of it one row lower.
to cantor :x :y :len :level
  if :level = 0 [stop]
  ; The color depends on the level (:level + 8 picks from colors 9
  ; to 15) so each row is easy to tell apart.
  ; FILLED walks a thin rectangle with the pen up and paints it in.
  ; A rectangle keeps its square corners, even when it is tiny.
  penup setxy :x :y setheading 90
  filled :level + 8 [repeat 2 [forward :len right 90 forward 16 right 90]]
  ; The left third starts where this bar starts.
  cantor :x :y - 40 :len / 3 :level - 1
  ; The right third starts two thirds of the way along.
  cantor :x + 2 * :len / 3 :y - 40 :len / 3 :level - 1
end

; ROWS draws the set with a heading label on top.
to rows :count
  cantor -360 150 720 :count
  setpencolor 0
  penup setxy -90 200 pendown
  setlabelheight 22
  label [The Cantor Set]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground 7
rows 7
